## Key Design Decisions

### Configurable condition
CONDITION in config.py drives everything. Changing it switches the target disease
across dataset labels, pos_weight calculation, checkpoint filenames, and print statements.
Valid values: 'Cardiomegaly', 'Effusion', 'Pneumonia', 'Nodule', 'Mass',
'Atelectasis', 'Consolidation', 'Edema', 'Emphysema', 'Fibrosis',
'Pleural_Thickening', 'Hernia', 'Pneumothorax', 'Infiltration'

### Class imbalance handling
BCEWithLogitsLoss with pos_weight = neg_count / pos_count computed from train_df.
Current cardiomegaly pos_weight ≈ 49.7 (1,536 positives out of 77,871 training images).

### Checkpoint resume
train.py automatically resumes from checkpoints/checkpoint_{condition}.pth if it exists.
Checkpoint saves model_state, optimizer_state, scheduler_state, epoch, best_val_loss, val_auc.

### Windows constraints
num_workers=0 in DataLoader — Windows multiprocessing causes hangs in both
Jupyter notebooks and .py scripts with num_workers > 0 on this machine.
Do NOT suggest changing num_workers > 0.

### No RLHF or LLM components
This is a pure computer vision classification pipeline.
Do not suggest LLM-based approaches, prompt engineering, or language model integration.

