## What NOT to suggest
- Do not suggest num_workers > 0
- Do not suggest training from scratch (pretrained=False)
- Do not suggest changing the dataset split from the official NIH split
- Do not suggest running on Kaggle or Google Colab — training runs locally
- Do not suggest LLM or multimodal approaches
- Do not suggest removing pos_weight — class imbalance is severe
- Do not suggest accuracy as a metric — dataset is severely imbalanced, AUC is the only valid metric

---

## What to prioritize when suggesting changes
1. Stability over complexity — simple changes that improve AUC without risking overfitting
2. Windows compatibility — all suggestions must work on Windows with num_workers=0
3. VRAM budget — RTX 4050 has 6GB, batch_size=32 at 224x224 uses ~0.5GB currently
4. Reproducibility — SEED=42 is set everywhere, maintain this
5. Modularity — keep changes isolated to the relevant file, don't mix concerns
